{"answer": "A tool with no row in the authority table is denied by default. `authorityOf` in `apps/api/src/oversight/toolAuthority.ts` treats it as `requires_human_action`, so it never executes. The oversight gate (`withHumanOversight`) never calls its executor. It returns the constant result `{\"error\":\"requires_human_action\",\"escalation\":\"blocked_consequential_call\"}` as a normal result, not a throw. The lookup only matches the table's own keys, so inherited property names like `toString` are denied too. The same default applies at both enforcement points. Separately, `assertAllToolsDeclared.ts` (FR-004) is meant to catch a registered tool that has no declared authority when the api starts. I read that last point from issue summaries and did not check the code.", "sources": ["specs/support-agent-human-oversight/spec.md (FR-003, FR-004)", "docs/human-oversight.md", "pull-280", "issue-445", "issue-448"]}
```

